-- | Halting the run, under every Host (plan 0.140 §3.4).
--
-- An operation into `Void` halts (D225/D227): nothing composed after it is
-- observed, and the run ends `halted`, one of the Spec's three ends with
-- `returned` and `exhausted` (D374). The end carries no value; a program that
-- wants something observed emits it first.
--
-- The signature is portable. Each Host supplies the code
-- (`Strata/Hosts/<host>/Interpretations/Halt.<arch>`) and its exit device's
-- status for `halted`: 2 under Linux and on `Bare/Virt`.
signature halt : Act Unit Void
